  "year": 2025,
  "arxivId": "2310.01405",
  "abstract": "This paper introduces representation engineering, a top-down approach to enhancing the transparency of AI systems by focusing on representations rather than neurons or circuits. The authors demonstrate the effectiveness of this approach in improving our understanding and control of large language models, particularly in areas such as honesty, hallucination, and power-seeking. They provide baselines and initial analysis of representation engineering techniques, showing their promise in tackling various safety-relevant problems.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "The Core Idea",
      "content": "The paper proposes a new approach to AI transparency called representation engineering (RepE), which places representations at the center of analysis rather than neurons or circuits. This top-down approach aims to understand and control high-level cognitive phenomena in neural networks. <strong>RepE</strong> draws insights from cognitive neuroscience, particularly the Hopfieldian view, which sees cognition as a product of representational spaces.",
