    {
      "title": "How It Works",
      "content": "The authors introduce a baseline technique called Linear Artificial Tomography (LAT) to extract neural activity related to target concepts or functions. <strong>LAT</strong> involves designing stimulus and task, collecting neural activity, and constructing a linear model to identify a direction that accurately predicts the underlying concept or function. This approach can be applied to various concepts, including truthfulness, utility, and morality.",
